### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### semantic-identifier-resolver — API walkthrough
###
### Run these with the IntelliJ HTTP Client (or the VS Code REST Client).
### Hosts come from http-client.env.json — pick the "dev" environment when
### prompted. Start the stack first (from the repository root):
###   docker compose --env-file .env.arangodb -f compose.yaml -p semantic-identifier-resolver up -d
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Gateway liveness
GET {{gateway}}/api/ping

### Worker liveness — each worker introduces itself: pong, its name and the
### contexts it replies to (worker.contexts).
GET {{worker1}}/api/ping

### Worker 2 liveness
GET {{worker2}}/api/ping

### Worker 3 liveness
GET {{worker3}}/api/ping

### ArangoDB version, via the gateway internals endpoint
GET {{gateway}}/api/internals/arangodb

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Full lookup, step 1: initiate (asynchronous request-reply)
### Answers 202 Accepted; resultsUrl in the body (and the Location header)
### points at the results URL. The requestHash is captured for the polling
### request below.
### A TAG lookup is answered by BOTH worker 1 (same-as: serial number and
### EPC descriptor) and worker 2 (part-of: the system) — the poll shows two
### claimedBy entries and two reply blocks.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "A-24HA001",
  "context": "TAG"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("requestHash", response.body.requestHash);
    client.log("Poll results at: " + response.headers.valueOf("Location"));
%}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Full lookup, step 2: poll the results URL
### 202 while pending/in_progress (claimedBy lists who signed up; partial
### results may already be present), 200 when done — a lookup is done only
### when EVERY claiming worker replied (or failed): results aggregates the
### distinct reply elements, resultsByWorker/failuresByWorker hold one block
### per worker — 500 when all claimants failed, 504 when timed out (partial
### results may be present). Shapes: schemas/lookup-state.schema.json.
### Re-run until the status flips to done. A repeat POST of the same lookup
### answers from the cache without re-queueing work.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gateway}}/api/lookup/results/{{requestHash}}

### Validation: blank id answers 400
POST {{gateway}}/api/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "  ",
  "context": "TAG"
}

### Unknown request hash answers 404
GET {{gateway}}/api/lookup/results/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### EPC descriptor lookup — answered by worker 3 alone: the serial number
### that is same-as the contractor's descriptor. Poll with the request
### below after a moment.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "EJ101A",
  "context": "EPC_DESCRIPTOR"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("requestHashEpc", response.body.requestHash);
%}

### Poll the EPC descriptor lookup
GET {{gateway}}/api/lookup/results/{{requestHashEpc}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Hard refresh: a repeat POST normally answers from the cache without
### queueing new work; the resultsHardRefresh header forces the lookup
### through the workers again (fresh claim, rebuilt replies).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/lookup
Content-Type: application/json
resultsHardRefresh: true

{
  "id": "A-24HA001",
  "context": "TAG"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### A context no worker covers: every worker ignores it, the request stays
### pending, and the gateway's timeout sweep answers 504 after
### lookup.timeout-seconds (60s by default).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/lookup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "X-999",
  "context": "NOBODY_HANDLES_THIS"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("requestHashOrphan", response.body.requestHash);
%}

### Poll the unhandled-context lookup: 202 while pending, 504 once swept.
### A new POST of the same lookup after the 504 re-queues it (retry).
GET {{gateway}}/api/lookup/results/{{requestHashOrphan}}
